{{Passive skill box|Chaos Inoculation}}

'''Chaos Inoculation''' (often referred to as '''CI''') is a [[keystone passive skill]] that grants immunity to [[chaos damage]], but sets maximum [[life]] to 1.

Although the character must survive entirely on [[energy shield]] instead of life, immunity to chaos damage can be a significant advantage.

==Interactions==
The chance and duration of both being [[stun]]ned and receiving an elemental [[status ailments]] is based on your maximum life '''before''' CI takes effect<ref>https://fr.pathofexile.com/forum/view-thread/18201/page/1</ref>. Maximum Life modifiers such as {{c|mod|increased maximum Life}}, {{c|mod|reduced maximum Life}}, etc. apply to the life before CI is applied. Since this base life value is then overwritten by CI, the only advantage life modifiers provide to a CI character is the reduction on stun and status ailment thresholds.

[[Low life]] conditions will never take effect while CI is enabled. Effects such as [[Pain Attunement]] and On Low Life mods on gear will not activate. For these effects, you must have 50% or less of your current maximum life. Chaos Inoculation sets your maximum life to 1. The exception to this is if you have {{il|Coward's Legacy}} equipped.

[[Full life]] conditions will always take effect because you are always at 100% of 1 life, making the condition of {{il|Damage on Full Life Support}} easy to maintain.

===Interaction with life reduction===
Life reductions apply before CI which sets life to 1. For example from {{il|Ephemeral Edge}}. Obtaining 100%+ reduced Maximum Life will not affect the 1 Life value.

===Blood Magic===
When linked with {{il|Lifetap Support}} or {{il|Arrogance Support}}, or while taking the [[Blood Magic]] Keystone or other similar effects, affected skills (including auras) cannot be cast, unless the skill has 0 Cost and/or Reservation. The mod {{c|mod|Skills Cost no Mana or Life while Focussed}} thus allows CI builds to cast skills with Life Costs (e.g. {{il|Reap}}, {{il|Corrupting Fever}} or {{il|Blood Rage}}).

===Chaos resistance reduction/penetration ===
Since CI grants a flat-out ''immunity'' to chaos damage, effects that reduce or penetrate chaos resistance (i.e. [[Occultist]]'s [[Void Beacon]]) have no effect against CI.<ref name="CIKiller"/>

===Being Poisoned===
Being Immune to Chaos Damage means that Chaos Damage cannot inflict poison (to the entity immune to chaos damage), although physical damage can still inflict poison.

==CI builds==
It is generally best to wait until you have high energy shield before taking CI because it's much easier to survive on life at lower levels. Don't be afraid to take life passive skills for survivability while leveling up, since you can remove them later. 

Characters with CI are usually more susceptible to [[stun]] and [[status ailments]] because of their low base life. Rather than taking otherwise useless life nodes as described above, Stun can be mitigated by obtaining Stun Immunity (e.g [[Vile Bastion]]), stacking Chance to Avoid Stuns, or through niche items such as {{il|Skyforth}} or {{il|Valyrium}}. Status ailments can be mitigated or avoided in a variety of different ways, including [[Pantheon Power]]s, {{il|Purity of Elements}}, Chance to Avoid Ailments, Reduced Effect/Duration of Ailments on You, or niche items such as {{il|Auxium}}.

Chaos Inoculation works well with some other keystone passives, such as:
* {{psl|Ghost Reaver}} converts sources of life leech into energy shield leech, at the cost of disabling ES recharge.
* {{psl|Zealot's Oath}} applies life regeneration to energy shield. The amount recovered is based on the same % of your max ES, rather than your max life. Flat regeneration recovers the same amount. Note that "regeneration" does not include life flasks, as they are just "Recovery".
* {{psl|Divine Shield}} can provide a large amount of regeneration to builds that also stack large amounts of Armour and Physical Damage Reduction.
* {{psl|Ghost Dance}} can instantly recover ES on builds that have a decent amount of Evasion, at the cost of capping your energy shield by your evasion rating.
* {{psl|id=wicked_ward_keystone2342}} can be used by builds relying on recharge, sacrificing some recharge rate for uninterruptible recharge.

