==Version history==
{{Version history table header}}
{{Version history table row|3.14.1|
* The in-game [[Character Screen]] now displays "Immune to Chaos Damage" if you have the '''Chaos Inoculation''' keystone passive skill allocated.
}}
{{Version history table row|3.14.0|
* Now does not change the displayed chaos resistance to 100%.<ref name="CI314"/>
}}
{{Version history table row|3.0.0|
* The passive skills behind Chaos Inoculation have been removed.
}}
{{Version history table row|2.3.2|
* Fixed an issue where players' life totals could get out of sync when they died from degeneration damage with Chaos Inoculation allocated.
}}
{{Version history table row|0.10.0|
* Chaos Inoculation now grants no additional energy shield bonus. Its complete immunity to chaos damage, synergy with Blood Rage and other skill combos are deemed sufficient upside to counteract the life penalty. 
}}
{{Version history table row|0.9.10e|
* The Chaos Inoculation keystone passive skill now grants +50% Energy Shield rather than +80%. 
}}
{{Version history table row|0.9.7d|
* Fixed the interaction between Chaos Inoculation and Blood Magic so that there's no crazy bugged death state any more. If you try to reserve life or mana when you have both of these keystones, you will now die properly. 
}}
{{Version history table row|0.9.6|
* Changed the Chaos Inoculation keystone so that your "real" life value is still used for checks related to stun and elemental status ailments. This will mean that you don't receive giant stuns/chills due to being reduced to 1 life. 
}}
{{Version history table row|0.9.5h|
* Chaos Inoculation now grants a multiplicative increase to Energy Shield. 
}}
{{Version history table row|0.9.5|
* Chaos Inoculation now grants +80% energy shield rather than +20% 
}}
{{Version history table row|0.9.4|
